WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.350 --> 00:00:02.570
I nearly pasted my whole mark

2
00:00:02.570 --> 00:00:03.710
sheet into a chatbot!

3
00:00:04.420 --> 00:00:08.280
Names, marks, even a note that Musa

4
00:00:08.280 --> 00:00:09.900
missed a month with sickle cell.

5
00:00:10.540 --> 00:00:11.500
Then I stopped.

6
00:00:12.250 --> 00:00:14.950
Where does all that go when I press send?

7
00:00:16.150 --> 00:00:17.910
Today: keeping pupils’ data

8
00:00:17.910 --> 00:00:19.890
private, and still using AI.

9
00:00:21.230 --> 00:00:23.590
When you press send, your words go

10
00:00:23.590 --> 00:00:24.670
to the company’s computers.

11
00:00:25.710 --> 00:00:27.750
There they’re processed, and

12
00:00:27.750 --> 00:00:29.150
usually stored for a while.

13
00:00:29.750 --> 00:00:31.450
Depending on the tool and settings,

14
00:00:31.990 --> 00:00:34.410
staff may review some chats, and

15
00:00:34.410 --> 00:00:36.150
chats may train later models.

16
00:00:37.520 --> 00:00:40.000
And what goes into training can come out.

17
00:00:40.660 --> 00:00:42.780
Models sometimes repeat pieces of

18
00:00:42.780 --> 00:00:44.620
their training text word for word.

19
00:00:45.290 --> 00:00:48.350
Researchers have pulled real names, phone

20
00:00:48.350 --> 00:00:50.910
numbers and emails out of models this way.

21
00:00:51.470 --> 00:00:54.050
It’s rare, but a pupil’s details typed

22
00:00:54.050 --> 00:00:56.430
today could turn up in someone else’s

23
00:00:56.430 --> 00:00:56.770
answer.

24
00:00:58.080 --> 00:01:01.140
Personal data is anything that points to a

25
00:01:01.140 --> 00:01:04.480
person, alone or with other details: a

26
00:01:04.480 --> 00:01:08.080
name, a face, a voice, an ID number.

27
00:01:08.690 --> 00:01:11.670
Even “the only girl in Primary Five with a

28
00:01:11.670 --> 00:01:13.970
hearing aid” points to one child.

29
00:01:15.290 --> 00:01:17.010
It’s like asking a teacher at

30
00:01:17.010 --> 00:01:17.990
another school for advice.

31
00:01:18.850 --> 00:01:20.970
You’d say, “One of my pupils

32
00:01:20.970 --> 00:01:22.270
keeps missing class.”

33
00:01:23.080 --> 00:01:25.280
Not her name and her family’s story.

34
00:01:25.950 --> 00:01:27.650
The advice is just as good.

35
00:01:28.850 --> 00:01:29.430
Quick check!

36
00:01:30.220 --> 00:01:32.160
Amina needs comments for

37
00:01:32.160 --> 00:01:34.200
sixty-two report cards.

38
00:01:35.000 --> 00:01:37.860
What’s the safest way to use AI?

39
00:01:39.210 --> 00:01:42.510
Swap names for Pupil A, B, C.

40
00:01:43.150 --> 00:01:44.890
Take out anything else that points

41
00:01:44.890 --> 00:01:48.150
to one child, and keep the key, who

42
00:01:48.150 --> 00:01:49.950
is who, on your own paper.

43
00:01:50.600 --> 00:01:53.040
Don’t count on deleting a chat later:

44
00:01:53.560 --> 00:01:55.280
copies may be kept for a while.

45
00:01:56.530 --> 00:01:58.950
Some things never go into a public

46
00:01:58.950 --> 00:02:01.390
AI tool, even to save time.

47
00:02:02.060 --> 00:02:04.540
Names with marks, health and special

48
00:02:04.540 --> 00:02:08.020
needs, family matters, photos and voice

49
00:02:08.020 --> 00:02:10.720
recordings, and ID or phone numbers.

50
00:02:12.030 --> 00:02:14.070
Before using any AI tool,

51
00:02:14.270 --> 00:02:15.770
check three things.

52
00:02:16.240 --> 00:02:18.460
Its settings: many let you switch

53
00:02:18.460 --> 00:02:19.780
off training on your chats.

54
00:02:20.550 --> 00:02:23.410
Its age rules: often thirteen and over,

55
00:02:23.870 --> 00:02:25.750
with a parent’s permission under eighteen.

56
00:02:26.490 --> 00:02:27.770
And your school’s rules:

57
00:02:28.410 --> 00:02:29.910
which tools, and for what.

58
00:02:31.210 --> 00:02:33.630
In the app, train a tiny language

59
00:02:33.630 --> 00:02:35.210
model on school sentences.

60
00:02:36.030 --> 00:02:38.490
Add a made-up private one, like

61
00:02:38.490 --> 00:02:41.150
“Halima has asthma”, and train again.

62
00:02:41.750 --> 00:02:44.670
Then let it write, again and again.

63
00:02:45.340 --> 00:02:47.340
If it picks the name, it writes your

64
00:02:47.340 --> 00:02:49.100
sentence back, word for word.

65
00:02:50.290 --> 00:02:50.830
Your turn.

66
00:02:51.440 --> 00:02:54.360
Why could a pupil’s details, typed into

67
00:02:54.360 --> 00:02:56.220
a chatbot, turn up again later?

68
00:02:57.510 --> 00:03:00.130
Chats can train later models, and

69
00:03:00.130 --> 00:03:01.890
models can repeat what they learned.

70
00:03:02.560 --> 00:03:05.060
Remember: some data never goes in.

71
00:03:05.640 --> 00:03:08.940
Swap names for Pupil A, B, C.

72
00:03:09.580 --> 00:03:11.520
And check the settings, age

73
00:03:11.520 --> 00:03:12.780
rules and school rules.

74
00:03:14.070 --> 00:03:15.390
Try it in class tomorrow:

75
00:03:15.730 --> 00:03:17.110
play “Traffic light”.

76
00:03:17.700 --> 00:03:20.920
Groups sort cards: a lesson topic,

77
00:03:21.340 --> 00:03:23.620
a test score with a name, a class

78
00:03:23.620 --> 00:03:25.400
photo, a pupil’s poem.

79
00:03:26.070 --> 00:03:28.330
Green: fine to share with AI.

80
00:03:29.110 --> 00:03:30.910
Amber: only without names.

81
00:03:31.650 --> 00:03:32.990
Red: never.

82
00:03:33.730 --> 00:03:35.830
Then discuss the hard cards.
